        <type>std::error_code</type>
        <definition>virtual std::error_code llvm::SectionMemoryManager::MemoryMapper::protectMappedMemory</definition>
        <argsstring>(const sys::MemoryBlock &amp;Block, unsigned Flags)=0</argsstring>
        <name>protectMappedMemory</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::SectionMemoryManager::MemoryMapper::protectMappedMemory</qualifiedname>
        <reimplementedby refid="classllvm_1_1anonymous__namespace_02_section_memory_manager_8cpp_03_1_1_default_m_mapper_1a7f9c28a81a61c5f292d14dbd7a9b2766">protectMappedMemory</reimplementedby>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="_a_arch64_promote_constant_8cpp_1a90f8350fecae261c25be85d38b451bff" kindref="member">const</ref> <ref refid="classllvm_1_1sys_1_1_memory_block" kindref="compound">sys::MemoryBlock</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>Block</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classunsigned" kindref="compound">unsigned</ref></type>
          <declname>Flags</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This method sets the protection flags for a block of memory to the state specified by <computeroutput>Flags</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The behavior is not specified if the memory was not allocated using the allocateMappedMemory method. <computeroutput>Block</computeroutput> describes the memory block to be protected. <computeroutput>Flags</computeroutput> specifies the new protection state to be assigned to the block.</para>
<para>If <computeroutput>Flags</computeroutput> is MF_WRITE, the actual behavior varies with the operating system (i.e. MF_READ | MF_WRITE on Windows) and the target architecture (i.e. MF_WRITE -&gt; MF_READ | MF_WRITE on i386).</para>
<para>\r error_success if the function was successful, or an error_code describing the failure if an error occurred. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
